---
import catalog from '../../../assets/materials/catalog.json';
import {asset} from '../data/catalog';
import {url} from '../lib/urls';
interface Props {path:string}
const {path}=Astro.props;
const materials=catalog.entries;
const variants=[
  {renderer:'mesh',phase:'dusk',id:'mesh-materials'},
  {renderer:'mesh',phase:'dawn',id:'library-mesh-dawn'},
  {renderer:'sdf',phase:'dusk',id:'library-sdf-dusk'},
  {renderer:'sdf',phase:'dawn',id:'library-sdf-dawn'},
];
const poster=asset('mesh-materials');const film=asset('mesh-materials-film');
---
<section class="section material-library" id="material-library" data-material-library>
  <span id="mesh-materials" class="anchor-target"></span>
  <div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">The complete library</span><h2>Twelve spheres. Changing light.</h2></div></div>
  <div class="library-controls" data-library-controls hidden><div class="renderer-controls" role="group" aria-label="Material renderer">
    <button class="filter" data-renderer="mesh" aria-pressed="true">Forward PBR</button>
    <button class="filter" data-renderer="sdf" aria-pressed="false">SDF ray marching</button>
  </div><div class="renderer-controls" role="group" aria-label="Lighting transition">
    <button class="filter" data-phase="dusk" aria-pressed="true">Dusk</button>
    <button class="filter" data-phase="dawn" aria-pressed="false">Dawn</button>
  </div></div>
  <figure class="scene-media library-stage"><div class="movie"><video data-library-film controls playsinline preload="none" poster={url(poster.file,path)} width={film.width} height={film.height} aria-label="Twelve material spheres · Forward PBR · dusk"><source src={url(film.file,path)} type="video/mp4"/><p><a data-library-download href={url(film.file,path)}>Download the film</a>.</p></video></div><figcaption class="media-foot" data-renderer-caption aria-live="polite">Forward PBR · dusk · native recorded playback</figcaption></figure>
  {variants.map(v=><a hidden data-material-variant data-renderer-key={v.renderer} data-phase-key={v.phase} href={url(asset(`${v.id}-film`).file,path)} data-poster={url(asset(v.id).file,path)}>{v.renderer} · {v.phase}</a>)}
  <p class="note">Both renderers use the same sphere layout, camera and lighting timeline. Glass shows how their light paths differ. Cloud drift is accelerated.</p>
  <a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/byebyebryan/cubey/blob/main/projects/pbr_materials/presets/presentation/README.md">Run the matched scenes ↗</a>
  <noscript><p class="note">Other films: {variants.slice(1).map(v=><a href={url(asset(`${v.id}-film`).file,path)}>{v.renderer==='sdf'?'SDF':'Forward PBR'} · {v.phase} · </a>)}</p></noscript>
  <details class="material-inspection"><summary>Inspect individual materials</summary><p class="note">Separate stills under frozen lighting. The order below matches the rows in the film.</p>
  <div class="material-grid">{materials.map(m=>{const mesh=asset(`library-mesh-${m.id}`);const sdf=asset(`library-sdf-${m.id}`);return <figure class="material-tile" data-material={m.id}>
    <a data-material-link href={url(mesh.file,path)} data-mesh={url(mesh.file,path)} data-sdf={url(sdf.file,path)} aria-label={`Open ${m.label} · Forward PBR`}><img data-material-image src={url(mesh.file,path)} data-mesh={url(mesh.file,path)} data-sdf={url(sdf.file,path)} data-label={m.label} width={mesh.width} height={mesh.height} alt={`${m.label} · Forward PBR mesh specimen`} loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></a>
    <figcaption><h3>{m.label}</h3><p>{m.description}</p></figcaption>
  </figure>;})}</div>
  <noscript><p class="note">SDF stills: {materials.map(m=><a href={url(asset(`library-sdf-${m.id}`).file,path)}>{m.label} · </a>)}</p></noscript></details>
  <details><summary>How the renderers share materials</summary><p class="note">Both use the same recipe library. Forward PBR shades mesh spheres; SDF ray marching shades implicit solids. SDF glass follows a bounded interface path and resolves to the environment, without refracting neighboring specimens. Frosted glass filters that environment light. These are matched lighting studies, rather than an equivalence test between optical solvers.</p><a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/byebyebryan/cubey/blob/main/docs/architecture/material-recipes.md">Shared recipes and renderer details ↗</a></details>
</section>
